  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Atlas Air recorded $480M in contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Atlas Air won 263 awards so far this fiscal year with an average award size of $1.8M. Obligations fell 36.8% year over year. Nonscheduled Chartered Passenger Air Transportation is the dominant market for Atlas Air, with $479M in obligations in FY2026 to date. Other reported markets include Other Technical and Trade Schools at $333K, Flight Training at $332K, and Scheduled Freight Air Transportation at $268K. Looking back across recent years, Atlas Air obligated $13.5M in FY21, $1.7M in FY22, $6M in FY23, $3.7M in FY24, and $759M in FY25. Current-year totals are partial because FY2026 is fiscal year to date. The mix and timing of awards produced a large year-over-year swing, concentrated in the Nonscheduled Chartered Passenger Air Transportation market.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Atlas Air's federal business trended year over year?",
        "body": "Atlas Air obligated $480M in FY2026 to date, down 36.8% year over year. Atlas Air's obligations peaked at $759M in FY25 and were $13.5M in FY21, $1.7M in FY22, $6M in FY23, and $3.7M in FY24. The large FY25 total versus the FY2026 to date total explains the reported year-over-year decline."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are Atlas Air's primary federal markets?",
        "body": "Nonscheduled Chartered Passenger Air Transportation is Atlas Air's primary market with $479M in FY2026 to date. Atlas Air also recorded $333K in Other Technical and Trade Schools, $332K in Flight Training, and $268K in Scheduled Freight Air Transportation."
      }
    ]
